  "subtitles": {
    "mode": "words",
    "words": "/Users/diplomat/ytvideos/channels/nuviko_history/videos/038_guy_fawkes/Edit/Production/v01/word_times_mix_v01.json",
    "transcript": "/Users/diplomat/ytvideos/channels/nuviko_history/videos/038_guy_fawkes/Source/Voice/tts_en_v01.txt",
    "phrases": [
      "On the night of November 5,",
      "1605, a man and barrels",
      "of gunpowder",
      "were discovered",
      "beneath the House of Lords",
      "in London.",
      "were discovered",
      "beneath the House of Lords",
      "in London.",
      "The man gave his name",
      "as John Johnson.",
      "His real name",
      "was Guy Fawkes.",
      "That same day,",
      "King James the First of England",
      "was due to attend",
      "the opening of Parliament.",
      "Members of both Houses",
      "would be gathered there",
      "with him.",
      "The people who had hidden",
      "the gunpowder",
      "planned to kill them all",
      "in a single explosion.",
      "But Fawkes was not",
      "the leader of the plot.",
      "And yet, centuries later,",
      "it is his name",
      "that millions of people",
      "still remember.",
      "Two years earlier,",
      "England had a new monarch.",
      "Many English Catholics",
      "hoped that James would ease",
      "the religious restrictions",
      "imposed under his predecessor,",
      "Elizabeth the First.",
      "Catholics faced fines",
      "and persecution,",
      "and Catholic priests",
      "were being hunted down.",
      "Those hopes for change",
      "were disappointed.",
      "So a small group of Catholics",
      "decided to take action.",
      "They did not represent",
      "all English Catholics.",
      "The plot was a decision",
      "made by specific individuals.",
      "The group was led",
      "by a nobleman named",
      "Robert Catesby.",
      "His plan was",
      "to blow up Parliament",
      "during its opening ceremony",
      "and kill the king.",
      "Guy Fawkes also joined",
      "the conspiracy.",
      "He was a soldier",
      "who had served",
      "in the Spanish army.",
      "His job was",
      "to guard the gunpowder",
      "and, when the time came,",
      "ignite it.",
      "But the explosion was only",
      "the beginning of their plan.",
      "The conspirators hoped",
      "to launch an uprising and seize",
      "the king's young daughter,",
      "Princess Elizabeth.",
      "They believed that",
      "once James was dead,",
      "they could bring about",
      "changes in the country.",
      "In 1605, the conspirators",
      "rented a space",
      "beneath the House of Lords",
      "and brought",
      "the gunpowder inside.",
      "The opening of Parliament",
      "had been postponed",
      "several times,",
      "but it was finally scheduled",
      "for November 5.",
      "Everything seemed ready.",
      "Then a letter appeared.",
      "On October 26,",
      "Lord Monteagle received",
      "an anonymous warning",
      "advising him",
      "not to attend Parliament.",
      "The letter reached",
      "the royal authorities.",
      "Who sent it remains unknown.",
      "Suspicion fell on",
      "one of the conspirators,",
      "a relative of Monteagle,",
      "but his authorship",
      "was never proven.",
      "The conspirators learned",
      "about the letter.",
      "Now there was a danger",
      "that the authorities",
      "would search the building",
      "and discover the gunpowder.",
      "Even so, they decided",
      "to go ahead.",
      "On the night before",
      "Parliament was due to open,",
      "the authorities",
      "conducted a search.",
      "They found Fawkes",
      "near the room",
      "containing the gunpowder",
      "and arrested him.",
      "The explosion never happened.",
      "While Fawkes was being",
      "questioned in London,",
      "Catesby and other conspirators",
      "tried to gather supporters",
      "outside the capital.",
      "But the large uprising",
      "they had hoped for",
      "never materialized.",
      "A few days later,",
      "the authorities caught up",
      "with the fugitives.",
      "Catesby was killed",
      "in a shootout.",
      "Fawkes was imprisoned",
      "in the Tower of London",
      "and interrogated.",
      "A royal order has survived",
      "authorizing the use",
      "of torture against him.",
      "In January 1606,",
      "Fawkes and the other",
      "surviving conspirators",
      "were executed.",
      "The conspirators had wanted",
      "to change the position",
      "of English Catholics.",
      "But after the plot failed,",
      "suspicion toward Catholics",
      "intensified,",
      "and the authorities",
      "introduced new requirements",
      "for their oath of allegiance.",
      "November 5 itself became",
      "a day of thanksgiving",
      "for the survival",
      "of the king and Parliament.",
      "Over time,",
      "a tradition developed in Britain",
      "of marking the day",
      "with bonfires and fireworks.",
      "People began burning",
      "effigies of Guy Fawkes",
      "on those bonfires.",
      "And so a man who",
      "had never led the conspiracy",
      "gave his name to a celebration",
      "that commemorates its failure."
